    2. Refining the _extract_unit Heuristic

        Your current implementation of _extract_unit is great, but we can make it even
        more "Tractor-proof" by handling the complex number space better. If a user
        types num("3 + 4j N"), rsplit(None, 1) will correctly grab N. However, if they
        type num("3 + 4j"), rsplit will grab 4j as the unit!

        The Fix: We should only treat the second part as a unit if it doesn't look like
        a complex component.

    3. The __eq__ and _normalize Harmony

        Currently, your __eq__ returns False if units don't match. This is technically
        correct but might be frustrating in a REPL. If I have x = num("12 in") and y =
        num("1 ft"), x == y should probably be True.

        Since you already have the excellent _normalize method, we can use it inside
        __eq__ to allow cross-unit equality checks.

    4. Code "Purity" Note on _binary_op

        In _binary_op, you have a target type check. When you get to the Winter Project
        of the C-extension, this is where the speed gains will happen. For now, ensure
        that self.real and self.imag are always mpmath.mpf (even for Int types) to
        prevent the "Ghost Digits" problem when you perform an operation that promotes a
        type.

