    ❓So, a good question is:  the internal numbers are immutable.  Is the unit string
    immutable too?  I think the answer needs to be "it's representation, no, but its
    'point' in the universe, yes."  In other words, you can change the unit to any
    conformable unit (e.g. barns or acres), but you can't change it to cubic meters.  So
    this means the unit checking machinery is fundamental to keeping it "physically
    immutable".  However, if you change the unit, the internal number components have to
    change to maintain the physical invariants.  So this means the hash computation has
    to do more than e.g. just hash the (self.real, self.imag, self.numer, self.denom,
    self.unit) tuple.  Maybe the hash has to be calculated using the "canonical basis
